Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 16:23:28 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] Fix #2: rebuild tracker.db only when SQLite says it is
 corrupt

OpenStore caught every exception and moved tracker.db aside, so a file
merely held by a backup tool, a database viewer or a second copy of the
app lost all local data on the next start.

- New DatabaseOpener (Data): opens the database, runs PRAGMA quick_check,
  and classifies failures. Only SQLITE_CORRUPT / SQLITE_NOTADB or a
  failed quick_check count as corrupt. SQLITE_BUSY / LOCKED / CANTOPEN
  and IOException sharing violations are "in use": retried 5x at 500 ms,
  then the app tells the person to close the other program and exits
  with code 1. Anything else keeps the file and runs in memory as before.
- SetAside copies tracker.db (+wal/+shm) to tracker.db.<stamp>.bad before
  a fresh one is started, and the dialog names the copy.

Tests: DatabaseOpenerTests - random bytes -> Corrupt and SetAside keeps
an identical copy; a file held with FileShare.None -> InUse, not renamed,
opens normally once released; error-code classification.

